+COCA List counts (17 September 2026): \mention{each has} 1,578, \mention{each was} 1,005, \mention{each will} 507, against \mention{every will} 12, \mention{every has} 8, \mention{every was} 3. The saved material contains 618 COCA lines with \mention{every} before a verb and 164 NOW lines for \mention{every was} and \mention{every has}. These are search totals, not matched opportunities for independent use or an estimate of its grammatical rate.
